# Postman API Testing Report

## Project Name
Secure & Optimized REST API

## Testing Tool
Postman

## Tested Endpoint
`GET /api/products?page=1&limit=2`

## Automated Response Validation Results

| # | Test Case | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Status code is 200 | PASS |
| 2 | Response is valid JSON | PASS |
| 3 | Success should be true | PASS |
| 4 | Pagination structure is correct | PASS |
| 5 | Products should be an array | PASS |
| 6 | Each product has valid fields | PASS |
| 7 | Cache header is present | PASS |

## Test Summary
- Total tests: 7
- Passed: 7
- Failed: 0

## Additional Verification
- Pagination response was verified.
- Cache response header was observed as `MISS` on the request tested.
- Authentication, authorization, invalid token, expired token, and product-not-found scenarios were tested separately.

## Conclusion
All seven automated response validation tests passed for the tested Products API request. Additional security scenarios were also tested separately.

**Note:** These results apply only to the scenarios tested; they do not guarantee that every API endpoint or edge case has been tested.
